<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθάδε</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ</span>], Adv.: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of Place, <i>thither, hither,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.492
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				304
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.36
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> after <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> more freq., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα</span>
			, <i>here</i> or <i>there,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθάδε αὐτοῦ μένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					765
				</span></i>
			; <i>in this world,</i> opp. the nether-world, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				525b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ᾽ εὔκολος μὲν ἐνθάδ᾽ εὔκολος δ᾽
					ἐκεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					82
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐ.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ κάτω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				923
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				75
			</span></i>; also, the people <i>of this country,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				42
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ἐνθάδ᾽ αὐτοῦ</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τις τῶν ἐνθάδ᾽ αὐτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					357
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐνθάδε,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐκεῖ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			circumstances, <i>in this case</i> or <i>state,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.4.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθάδ᾽ ἥκων</span> having come
				<i>to this point,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				377
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοῦ πάθους</span>
			<i>at this stage</i> of my suffering, ib. <i><span class="en">
				899
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of Time,
				<i>here, now,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἐνθάδ᾽ ὁρῶν οὔτ᾽
			ὀπίσω</span> neither <i>the present</i> nor the future, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				488
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτίκ᾽ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					992
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
